pulsar (1.133.1-0parrot5) echo; urgency=medium

  * Skip dh_shlibdeps and dh_makeshlibs: the shipped tree is a prebuilt
    vendor bundle with foreign-arch binaries and a private-rpath git, so
    dependencies are declared explicitly in debian/control.
  * Prune development dependencies from the shipped node_modules; the
    electron package would otherwise ship a second copy of the runtime.

 -- Lorenzo "Palinuro" Faletra <palinuro@parrotsec.org>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:34:38 +0100

pulsar (1.133.1-0parrot4) echo; urgency=medium

  * Restrict architectures to amd64, arm64 and armhf; upstream publishes
    no riscv64 Electron runtime, so the build cannot run there.

 -- Lorenzo "Palinuro" Faletra <palinuro@parrotsec.org>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:42:39 +0100

pulsar (1.133.1-0parrot3) echo; urgency=medium

  * Skip dh_strip: the Electron runtime and vendored helpers ship
    prebuilt and pre-stripped, with foreign-arch ELFs that break
    stripping.

 -- Lorenzo "Palinuro" Faletra <palinuro@parrotsec.org>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:39:14 +0100

pulsar (1.133.1-0parrot2) echo; urgency=medium

  * Set HOME to an in-tree directory during the build; electron
    install.js and yarn need a writable HOME, which sbuild does not
    provide.

 -- Lorenzo "Palinuro" Faletra <palinuro@parrotsec.org>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:11:02 +0100

pulsar (1.133.1-0parrot1) echo; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Include the ppm submodule (pinned at f29fd1d) in the upstream source
    tarball.
  * Rebuild native modules against the pinned Electron 32.3.3 runtime,
    fetched at build time.
  * Bootstrap Yarn Classic from npm at build time; the v1 lockfile is
    not readable by the distro yarnpkg.

 -- Lorenzo "Palinuro" Faletra <palinuro@parrotsec.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:56:54 +0100
